  <api>alpha</api>
 </stability>
 <license uri="https://opensource.org/licenses/MIT">MIT</license>
 <notes>0.4.2: session settings are request-wide, as the RFC specifies: session_name(), session_set_cookie_params(), session_cache_limiter() and ini_set() of session.* change them for every scope, and a new scope's save handler is the current session.save_handler; only the session itself (id, status, save handler state, $_SESSION) is per scope. Switching scopes is faster: a generator step that crosses scopes went from about 530 ns to about 230 ns (the locale is written only when it differs, and the superglobal entries are found through a cached bucket). The README notes that two scopes opening the same session id with a locking save handler (files, memcached, redis) deadlock the process.</notes>
